WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
This Loss concerns FireSat
tutorial reports in the

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.740 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Payload Operating Environment.

3
00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:08.920 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Before building its tree, we
identify where that asset is held or

4
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.120 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
transported in each relevant state.

5
00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:14.420 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
These relationships determine
which system elements appear in

6
00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:15.500 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
the initial structure.

7
00:00:15.674 --> 00:00:19.060 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
In Asset Manager, expand
the tutorial asset row.

8
00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:24.060 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Set Trace relationship type to HOLDS,
choose Standby as the State context,

9
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.420 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
and select Payload Processor
in Multi-select entities.

10
00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:31.880 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Review that pairing and choose
Allocate, showing one selected entity.

11
00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:34.380 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
This action saves the trace immediately.

12
00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:38.520 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
For the second assignment, choose
TRANSPORTS and the Imaging state,

13
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.280 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
then select Payload Downlink Feed Interface.

14
00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:42.940 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Choose Allocate again.

15
00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:45.900 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
We have described two different
asset relationships in

16
00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:47.440 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
their operational contexts.

17
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:51.980 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
A trace in one state does not
automatically apply in every other state.

18
00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:56.460 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Return to the Loss Tool and use
Reload slash reconcile to refresh its

19
00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:58.140 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
previously loaded Core view.

20
00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:02.120 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Open Trace coverage and confirm two
of two environment states are covered,

21
00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.820 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
with the intended entities.

22
00:01:03.962 --> 00:01:06.180 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Coverage establishes model participation;

23
00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:09.380 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
it does not establish that
either state is secure.

24
00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:12.960 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Select Auto-build and wait for
the built-and-committed message.

25
00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:16.240 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
This operation writes immediately,
without waiting for the

26
00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:17.320 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
canvas Commit button.

27
00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:21.240 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Use Fit tree to inspect the
environment, states, entities,

28
00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:23.800 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
and any existing canonical attack branches.

29
00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:27.860 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
The generated structure is a starting
point for analysis and refinement.

30
00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:31.860 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
At the upper right of the canvas,
select Nocturne for dark mode,

31
00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:33.440 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
then Parchment to return.

32
00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.600 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
This changes presentation only.
